          "id": "mt-q-triad",
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "A chart says D. Which notes make the D major triad?",
          "options": [
            "D F A",
            "D F# A",
            "D G A",
            "D F# A#"
          ],
          "answer": 1,
          "explanation": "Major is 4 then 3 half steps. D up 4 is F# (D#, E, F, F#), and F# up 3 is A (G, G#, A). D F A is D minor; D F# A# has an augmented fifth."
        },
